course: dictionary
lesson: 2022
title: Confession: owning up and telling the truth
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A confession is when you admit that you did something, often something wrong. «I have a confession to make: I broke the window.» The clue is "I have a confession to make," so the speaker is owning up to a mistake.
explain: The same word can mean different things in different places. In church, a confession can be telling your sins to God, often with a priest listening. In a court or a police station, a confession is a statement that a person did a crime. Read the words around it to know which meaning fits.
explain: A confession can also be a light, shy secret. «I have a confession: I don't like cake.» Nobody did anything wrong there. Ask yourself: is this about wrongdoing, a holy act, or a secret? Then choose the meaning that fits the clues.
fact: A confession is when you admit that you did something wrong.
fact: In some churches, confession means telling your sins to God, often with a priest listening.
fact: In law, a confession is a statement to the police or a court that a person did a crime.
fact: Many people feel real relief after confession, like a weight lifted off their shoulders.
fact: Phrases to know: make a confession, go to confession, a full confession, I have a confession to make.
exercise: «Many people feel real relief after confession, like a weight lifted.» What does this sentence tell us about confession? | *It can bring real relief | It is a type of sweet | It is a race | It always makes you cry
exercise: Mia says, «I have a confession: I don't like cake.» What kind of confession is this? | A statement to the police | A crime | A prayer in church | *A shy secret, told lightly
exercise: «A confession that excuses itself is half a confession,» says the vicar. What does the vicar mean? | *Someone who makes excuses has not fully owned up | Vicars never make mistakes | Excuses are always the best | A confession must be sung
test: «Shame again, and a second confession.» What does a second confession mean here? | A prize for being brave | A new game | *Owning up to a wrong for a second time | A lost letter
test: In a court, what is a confession? | A kind of holiday | A list of shopping | *A statement that a person did a crime | A song sung in church
exam: Which is a confession to a police officer? | A child says sorry to her teacher for being late | *A suspect tells the police that he did the crime | A boy says he loves football | A girl tells her mum her favourite colour
